{
  "$comment": "AUTHORITY for the media types a knowledge base admits, and what the system can do with each. A row's `mediaType` is a member of the `SupportedMediaType` schema, and every member has exactly one row: the generators refuse a registry and an enum that disagree. Admission is membership: every row is storable, nameable and uploadable. The capabilities say what more there is. `render` is the viewer a reader mounts (`none`: metadata and a download). `anchoring` is the annotation model: character-offset text selectors, or spatial geometry. `textSource` is where a type's text comes from: decoded from its own bytes, derived by reading them (`pdf-text-layer`), or nowhere. `authorable` types are offered where a person writes a resource, and a clone keeps its source's type only when it is one. `generatable` types are ones the generation worker can produce. `application/pdf` is one because the worker compiles Typst the model writes. Every row whose `render` and `anchoring` are `none` is stored, named and downloadable and nothing more: a deliberate admission, promoted by editing its row. `extension` is the one a stored name takes, with its dot. ROW ORDER MATTERS: two types that share an extension (.xml, .yaml, .js, .ts, .webm) resolve, from the extension, to the first row that states it. The video rows are before the audio rows so that .webm is video. `extensionAliases` are other spellings of an extension a file may carry, each with the extension a row states that it is read as. TypeScript: scripts/spec/generate-media-types.mjs writes packages/core/src/generated/media-types.ts. Rust: packages/sdk-rust/build.rs writes `semiont::media_types`. Go: scripts/spec/generate-media-types-go.mjs writes packages/sdk-go/mediatypes/registry_gen.go, which is committed and checked for drift in CI. The rules read from this table (which format a clone takes, the name content is stored under) are held in every SDK by cases.json.",
  "render": ["text", "image", "pdf", "none"],
  "anchoring": ["text-selector", "spatial", "none"],
  "textSource": ["decode", "pdf-text-layer", "none"],
  "extensionAliases": {
    ".markdown": ".md",
    ".htm": ".html",
    ".jpeg": ".jpg",
    ".yml": ".yaml"
  },
